//www.meetup.com/tough-guy-book-club/events/315971420/","description":"Join us for the Toronto Chapter of Tough Guy Book Club.\nYou can find out this month's book here [https://toughguybookclub.com/books](https://toughguybookclub.com/books?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExcTVleWRsd0ZYSWdqZXV4QXNydGMGYXBwX2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR5aL8E3xpn05czDIaY5kEiHH3oABs4hICFLOrNXUsW-0gY5HePBTW1ni0SYzw_aem_qNxAzG9ij-sVr5-Rf8Uw3Q)\nIf you have the chance, try to pick up the book and read a couple of pages before the night. If you haven’t, come anyway, no one gives a damn. We are not your boss.\nIf you got one, make sure to bring your copy of the books down, it’ll help you talk about bits of it, we suggest underlining stuff that sticks out to you as important.\nAlso like all months, we will be announcing next month’s book at the meeting and handing them out to those of you who were wise enough to pre-order last month.\nSee you there.\nWant to know more about Tough Guy Book Club? Read this -\n[http://toughguybookclub.com/about-us](http://toughguybookclub.com/about-us?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAYnJpZBExcTVleWRsd0ZYSWdqZXV4QXNydGMGYXBwX2lkEDIyMjAzOTE3ODgyMDA4OTIAAR5QrDxxQmsaiuIfgbomTP4b6948UogKCm9U4Dudq5-VU_8aUx5RnTiUjO_R1Q_aem_n5AIic3b6NMTZ5TUJGTLkw)","startDate":"2026-10-07T08:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto ON","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1301 Queen Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Tough Guy Book Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tough-guy-book-club/"},"performer":"Tough Guy Book Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"SENIORS ACTIVE LIVING FAIR","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-seniors-social-club/events/316653919/","description":"Join me at this ACTIVE LIVING FAIR on October 7th AT THE YONGE\nEGLINTON COMMUNITY CENTRE.\nFree Refreshments while they last so bring your own water, just in case.\n\n**FOR MORE INFO. CONTACT:**\nSTACEY G. - 416-391-0511 EXT 237 or\nolderadults@yongeeglintoncc.com\nPlease check out details of featured events in photos below. Our thanks\nto Daniel Krasner for the advance notice to this informative event. : )","startDate":"2026-10-07T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"160 Eglinton Avenue East","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"160 Eglinton Ave E, Toronto, ON M4P 3B5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Seniors Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-seniors-social-club/"},"performer":"Toronto Seniors Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"On Stalking: Objectification and Self-Concealment","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316757070/","description":"This talk sets out to answer two questions: 1. What is the bare wrong of stalking? By bare wrong I mean the wrongness of **stalking as such** rather than the wrongs that often accompany it such as assault or intimidation. And 2. Why or what about stalking makes it hard to see it for what it is? This talk argues that the bare wrong of stalking is **objectification**. The stalker who merely watches their victim, the stalker who contacts their victim, the stalker who intimidates and threatens their victim, and the stalker who escalates to violence all objectify their victim. Recognizing the bare wrong as objectification maintains the conceptual unity of stalking and also makes sense of why stalking escalates, often to violence and sometimes murder.\n\nMy talk also explains an important but underexamined feature of stalking: its tendency to be **self-concealing**. By this I mean that stalking can obscure its own wrongness from the victim and from third parties even when the stalker's conduct occurs openly.\n\nMaggie O'Brien\nhttps://profiles.laps.yorku.ca/profiles/mjobrien/\nAssistant Professor\nDepartment of Philosophy\nYork University\n\n**About the Speaker:**\n\nI research and teach in feminist, legal, and political philosophy. I am particularly interested in the questions that come up at the intersection of these areas. My current work is on standing — both legal standing and moral and political standing. Standing (to a first approximation) means the right to perform certain sorts of speech-acts. I am developing a feminist case for a sceptical view about the value of standing norms according to which they are pernicious, especially to women and other marginalized groups.\n\nI am the recipient of a SSHRC Insight Development Grant (2026-2028) for my project Standing, Politics, and Disagreement. Before starting at York, I taught at the University of Edinburgh in both the Law School and Philosophy Department. I received my PhD in philosophy from McMaster University in 2016 and completed a Masters in Studies in Law from the University of Toronto in 2017.\n\n**\\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\***\n\nThis is a talk with audience Q&A presented by the University of Toronto's Centre for Ethics that is free to attend and open to the public. Free refreshments will be provided at the event. The talk will also be streamed online with live chat here [to be posted].\n\nAbout the Centre for Ethics (http://ethics.utoronto.ca):\n\nThe Centre for Ethics is an interdisciplinary centre aimed at advancing research and teaching in the field of ethics, broadly defined. The Centre seeks to bring together the theoretical and practical knowledge of diverse scholars, students, public servants and social leaders in order to increase understanding of the ethical dimensions of individual, social, and political life.\n\nIn pursuit of its interdisciplinary mission, the Centre fosters lines of inquiry such as (1) foundations of ethics, which encompasses the history of ethics and core concepts in the philosophical study of ethics; (2) ethics in action, which relates theory to practice in key domains of social life, including bioethics, business ethics, and ethics in the public sphere; and (3) ethics in translation, which draws upon the rich multiculturalism of the City of Toronto and addresses the ethics of multicultural societies, ethical discourse across religious and cultural boundaries, and the ethics of international society.\n\nThe Ethics of A.I. Lab at the Centre For Ethics recently appeared on a list of 10 organizations leading the way in ethical A.I.: https://ocean.sagepub.com/blog/10-organizations-leading-the-way-in-ethical-ai","startDate":"2026-10-07T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Larkin Building, Room 200","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"15 Devonshire Place, University of Toronto, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Coffee & Conversation @ Sheppard Yonge Sheppard Centre","url":"https://www.meetup.com/authentic-friendships-toronto/events/315893993/","description":"Join us for a casual coffee meet-up where we can share stories, and enjoy great conversation in a relaxed atmosphere.\nThis is a perfect opportunity to connect with members of the group, build friendships, and be part of our growing community. Whether you’re new to the group or have been with us for a while, this is a friendly, welcoming space for everyone.\n\n**Event:** Social Gathering for both men and women\n**Location:** Yonge Sheppard Centre - 4841 Yonge St, North York, ON\n\n**Arrival Time:** 1:30-2pm\n**End Time**: Anytime\n\nBring a smile and great conversation and let's make it a fun, easygoing get together.\n\nAttendance - Must confirm with Host if joining by msg or comment.","startDate":"2026-10-07T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Sheppard Center (Yonge Sheppard Subway) Food Court (lower level)","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4841 Yonge St., Toronto, ON, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Authentic Friendships Language Exchange","url":"https://www.meetup.com/authentic-friendships-toronto/"},"performer":"Authentic Friendships Language Exchange"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316602043/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-07T20:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"CELPIP Preparation Meet up","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-international-friends-meetup-group/events/316615621/","description":"This is a study meet up to prepare for CELPIP exam.\nAnyone is welcome!","startDate":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"[Toronto] ESL Cafe | English Conversation Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-international-friends-meetup-group/"},"performer":"[Toronto] ESL Cafe | English Conversation Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Magic the Gathering: Going Commander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/316601946/","description":"Every Wednesday Night!\nFree Magic The Gathering Commander games at Hairy Tarantula, hosted by Toronto Gaymers!\n\nPlease note: Masks are required in store!\n\nFor more information and to RSVP please over to harryt.com/events","startDate":"2026-10-07T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hairy Tarantula","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"3456 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free English Classes  - in-person at our Toronto school ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/events/316601962/","description":"Practise your English in a friendly, welcoming class in Toronto.\nJoin our free in-person English class and improve your speaking, fluency, grammar and vocabulary with supportive teachers. This class is a great opportunity to practise English, build confidence and meet new people.\n\n**When**\nEvery weekday Monday - Friday\n2.00pm–4.00pm\n\n**Where**\nTeaching House Toronto\nOHC / Sol Camps\n469 Jarvis St\nToronto, ON M4Y 2G8\nCanada\n\n[REGISTER NOW](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)\n\n**What you’ll practise**\n\n* Speaking and fluency\n* Grammar and vocabulary\n* Listening and pronunciation\n* Everyday English for real-life situations\n* Confidence using English with other people\n\n**Who can join?**\nAdults aged 18+ who want to improve their English. Refugees, asylum seekers and newcomers are very welcome.\n\n**About the classes**\nThe classes are taught by trainee English teachers on a Cambridge-accredited CELTA course and supervised by experienced teacher trainers.\n\n**Cost**\nFree\n\n**Before the class**\nPlease arrive a little early so we can welcome you and check your English level.\nSpaces may be limited, so please RSVP if you would like to attend.Cost: FREE\n\nSign up using this [registration form ](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)for automatic reminders and to be on our list for future classes.","startDate":"2026-10-07T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Teaching House Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"469 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/"},"performer":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Google Agentic AI Builder Lab - Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aittg-toronto/events/316770660/","description":"**Important Notes:** Register on the [AICamp](https://www.aicamp.ai/event/eventdetails/W2026100715) is required for admission. RSVP on meetup is turned off.\n\nBuilding Next Gen Autonomous Agentic Systems with Google - Toronto\n\nJoin Google and AICamp for an intensive, in-person build lab where theory translates directly into functional software. Most AI tutorials stop at simple single-turn prompts, but scalable systems require autonomous agents that reason over live data, manage persistent context, and execute complex multi-step tasks. In this hands-on workshop, you will step beyond conversational interfaces to architect, configure, and deploy next-generation autonomous agentic systems using Google Cloud.\n\nBring your laptop! This is an active engineering session with zero local setup required. You will leave with a fully functioning system running in your cloud environment.\n\n**What We'll Do:**\n\n* Autonomous Task Orchestration: Configure multi-step agent workflows that plan, reason, and act across complex task flows.\n* State & Tool Integration: Connect agent architectures to cloud tools, execution environments, and live datasets.\n* Resilient System Design: Implement robust patterns built to manage complex runtime inputs, long-running processes, and error recovery.\n\n**Agenda:**\n\\- 5:00pm\\~5:30pm: Checkin\\, food and networking\n\\- 5:30pm\\~7:30pm: Hands\\-on workshop/Code labs\n\\- 7:30pm\\~8:00pm: Build your own projects\n\\- 8:00pm\\~8:30pm: Demo\\, Open discussion and Mixer\n\n**Hands-on Workshop: Building Resilient Asynchronous Agents**\nMoving beyond conversational chatbots requires systems that do more than predict the next token. Real-world autonomous architectures must plan multi-step operations, interface with external tools, maintain state across asynchronous operations, and recover cleanly from runtime failures.\nIn this intensive 90-minute, in-person masterclass, you will move directly into active engineering. Working entirely inside Google Cloud Shell, you will build and deploy a next-generation autonomous agentic system from the ground up—wiring dynamic tool calling, state management, and resilient multi-step orchestration into a cohesive, runnable architecture.\nNo slides, no abstract theory, and zero local setup required. Bring your laptop, build alongside Google engineers, and leave with a fully functional autonomous system running live in the cloud.\n\n**Sponsors:**\nWe are actively seeking sponsors to support AI developers community. Whether it is by offering venue spaces, providing food, or cash sponsorship. Sponsors will not only speak at the meetups, receive prominent recognition, but also gain exposure to our extensive membership base of 10,000+ AI developers in Toronto or 500K+ worldwide.","startDate":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"George Brown College - Casa Loma Campus, 160 Kendal Avenue, Toronto, ON M5R 1M3","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"Location  160 Kendal Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto AI Developers Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aittg-toronto/"},"performer":"Toronto AI Developers Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Spanish Classes (In-Person)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/events/316602267/","description":"**Spanish in Mississauga - Introduction to Spanish**\nNew beginner Spanish language classes in Mississauga\n\nIn this class, we will explore the Spanish language through 8 modules. We will cover basic concepts which you need to know in any Spanish-speaking country, and we will begin speaking right away and practicing in groups by module 3.\n\nThe goal is that you gain a basic understanding of the language. Weekly homework is required and active participation is encouraged.\n\n**These classes are not free.** Please consider watching an information session to learn more about the structure and how you can be part of this learning community.\n**Costs:** In-person registration can be made during the first class, and you can pay all classes at once without incurring payment fees (on this platform). You can also register for all classes right here on Eventbrite.\n\n**Date:** We will host weekly beginner Spanish classes weekly, for four (4) weeks:\n\n* October 7\n* October 14\n* October 21\n* October 28\n\nWe may offer a class social - practice in a group setting, restaurant or venue TBD.\nThis is your opportunity to learn language in only four classes!\n\n**Time**: Classes will begin at 5:30pm and will end at 6:30pm.\n\n**Location:** Mississauga Valley Community Centre\nClasses will be held in-person .\n\nPlease ensure that you participate in all four (4) classes, as we have already covered pronunciation and are practicing with our peers by class 2.\n\nIf you cannot attend all classes, consider joining us next month. We will continue to offer them on the first 4 Wednesdays of each month - participation in all classes is mandatory.\n\n**The instructor**\nMeet Rohit (Vic) Mehta- a fluent spanish speaker who has been a private tutor since 2014. He is continuing the popular Beginner Spanish Class series which was offered during pre-Covid times.\n\nWe hope to see you there! If you have any questions, please don't hesitate to contact us! Email dogoodspanish@gmail.com\n\n**Frequently Asked Questions:**\n\n**Do the classes have a cost?**\nYes, classes cost 20 each + fees (if paying online). You can also contribute cash or pay by interac e-transfer. There is an additional textbook available for purchase for 20.\n\n**How long are the classes?**\nClasses are held in-person for one (1) hour per week x 4 weeks. At the end of the weekly sessions, we will invite you to a social on a separate evening or weekend.\n\n**What should I bring?**\nA water bottle, snack, notebook and pen.\n\n**Is free parking available?**\nYes, the Mississauga Valley Community Centre has ample parking, and is also very accessible by transit.\n\n**Can I bring a friend?**\nYes absolutely, however all participants need to pay as an individual. We will credit you one (1) FREE class for bringing a friend.\n\n**Can I bring my kids?**\nNo, this is an adult only class. The themes are fast-paced and we want all participants to feel comfortable. We can make exceptions for older teenagers.\n\n**What if I miss a class?**\nIt is recommended that you attend all four (4) classes in the series. We can make a rare exception and offer a paid, Zoom class, for extreme circumstances.\n\n**What if I already took a beginner class?**\nConsider joining our Intermediate Class 4-part series, from 6:40pm to 7:40pm, beginning on the first Wednesday of each month.","startDate":"2026-10-07T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Mississauga Valley Community Centre, Hazel MacCallion Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1275 Mississauga Valley Blvd., ON L5A 3R8, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/"},"performer":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"TOPHATs Village Idiots and Rock Stars at the AGO","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316750567/","description":"Join Lawrence, your top hatted host for and evening of Beer and Free Entry to the AGO.\n\nOn Monday, get your FREE pass to the AGO by following this link.\n\nhttps://ago.ca/visit/free-wednesday-night\n\nAt 6 pm, we will Meet-up at the Village Idiot for our social. They have a great selection of import and craft beers. Lots of good local dishes to enjoy.\n\nAt 7 pmish, we will cross the street to the AGO to gain FREE entry. I recommend taking a screen shot of your pass on your phone to enable fast access.\n\nOur first exhibit will be\nMelissa Auf der Maur: My ‘90s Rock Photographs on\nhttps://ago.ca/exhibitions/melissa-auf-der-maur-my-90s-rock-photographs\n\nThen we will meander our way over to the The Marvin Gelber Print and Drawing Study Centre, where we will see prints, drawings and photographs.\n\nhttps://ago.ca/research/print-and-drawing-centre","startDate":"2026-10-07T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Village Idiot Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"126 McCaul St M5T 1W2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Coming Out, Being Out - Peer Discussion (Weekly)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/events/316602670/","description":"**Description**\n\nComing Out Being Out (COBO) is a peer discussion group that has served the LGBT community for over 15 years in downtown Toronto. We meet to share stories and opinions, challenges and triumphs at all stages of coming out and being out.\n\nCOBO participants are lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, two-spirit and questioning people. We welcome all who identify under the banner of queer sexual orientation and gender identity.\n\n**What We Do**\n\n\\|\\-\\| COBO participants are often seeking to:\n\n* Understand what experiences others have in coming out to family, friends and their respective communities.\n* Develop comfort in discussing their identity with others.\n* Meet others having the same experiences when it comes to living openly.\n* Receive the encouragement of peers.\n\n\\|\\-\\| Regular topics of discussion include:\n\n* How people choose to come out (at work, with family, with friends).\n* Where to find others like us in the community.\n* Challenges and triumphs in navigating family and partner relationships.\n\n**Where & When**\n\n* Every Wednesday from 6-8pm\n* Community meeting space at Casey House - 119 Isabella St., Toronto\n\n**How to Access the Meeting**\n\nRegistration on Meetup is not required to attend. Attendance is on a drop-in basis. The front door to our meeting space at Casey House is controlled by the main floor receptionist. To access the space when you arrive:\n\n* Press the button to the left of the main entrance door.\n* Tell the receptionist that you are there for the COBO meeting.\n* You will be buzzed in and someone from our group will come to show you to the meeting.\n\nWE LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING YOU ON WEDNESDAY!\n\n*COBO is a community group led by non-professional peer facilitators and is not a Casey House program.*","startDate":"2026-10-07T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Casey House - Community Meeting Space","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"119 Isabella Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/"},"performer":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://s